# Byte-exactness is the product here, not a style preference.
#
# probe-harness.py recomputes the sha256 of AutoStemProbe/__init__.py from disk on every run and
# exits 2 on a mismatch, and every recorded hash in this folder (README, HARNESS, the acceptance
# sets) was measured against LF-only bytes. The repo is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# and has no root .gitattributes, so without this file a fresh checkout rewrites these LF blobs to
# CRLF: AutoStemProbe/__init__.py grows from 26,112 to 26,662 bytes, its digest stops matching the
# pin, and the harness that is supposed to prove the probe safe to run redders on a clean clone.
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose - a root .gitattributes would touch the 23 tracked files
# other lanes are editing, and renormalizing a shared tree is not this commit's business.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pyc binary
